claimed: match-moves-out — okay-match leaves the public library, at the
operator's decision: the matching marketplace is a commercial product
and not part of what this repository offers.

TOUCHING build.sbt, which this repo flags for coordination, and
REMOVING modules. okay-match (15 files) goes; okay-demo loses ChatDemo,
TwoNode and TestChatDemo, which are demos OF the marketplace; and the
two single-test modules okay-demo-e2e-browser and okay-demo-embed go
whole, since each contains nothing but a chat-demo test.

Nothing else in the library imports okay.matching -- checked rather
than assumed. okay-demo keeps Combine, DemoDeploy, IndexReport,
IntentRouter, Login, RepoAgent, RepoMcp and StateMcp, none of which
touch it.

Documentation: docs/modules/okay-match.md and specs/match.md go, and
the mentions in twelve other files are removed. The module dependencies
stay public and unchanged -- okay-rag, okay-agent, okay-sql and
okay-persist keep every other caller they have.

The code is moved WITH ITS HISTORY into the private repository first
and verified building there, before anything is deleted here.
